Condensed from: Steefel, C. I., CrunchFlow: Software for Modeling Multicomponent Reactive Flow and
Transport, User's Manual, Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory, October 12, 2009 (91 pages).
https://www.netl.doe.gov/sites/default/files/netl-file/CrunchFlow-Manual.pdf

Kept (manual pages): reaction rate laws (11-12), units (25-26), species choice, redox, acid-base,
activity model, initialization and temperature (27-29), keyword blocks and units (31), RUNTIME
chemistry keywords (35, 38-39, 42), PRIMARY_SPECIES through INITIAL_CONDITIONS (47-71),
TEMPERATURE/set_temperature (85).
Dropped: numerical methods, program structure, boundary conditions, discretization, output,
transport, flow, porosity, PEST, erosion.
Equations were transcribed from page images (the PDF's equation fonts have no Unicode mapping).
The manual's older program names GIMRT/OS3D are written as CrunchFlow.
